Subject: [PATCH 04/10] feat(failover): retry a dead CDN mirror instead of
 never playing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

B站 hands out `baseUrl` plus 1-2 `backupUrl` mirrors per audio stream, but the
shared resolver keeps only `baseUrl`, so a single unreachable CDN host means the
track never plays ("[RJKM] format error encountered; this could indicate
network errors"). RJKM also returns early for those errors and never reports
them to the app, so nothing upstream ever retries.

  * new src/utils/mediafetch/biliAudioFailover.ts — ask playurl again, collect
    baseUrl + backupUrl[] (cached per song) and walk the mirrors
  * usePlayback watches the <audio> element directly (error + a 20s stall
    watchdog) because RJKM swallows network errors, and on failure swaps in the
    next mirror for the *same* track (max 3 tries), then moves on to the next
    song only when the mirrors are exhausted
  * the gain pipeline is re-attached to the retried stream

Sampling polish in the same pass:
  * wait until *that* stream is playing before sampling (don't fight the first
    byte for bandwidth); skip entirely when playback already failed
  * retry once after 20s while the track plays — CDN hiccups are transient
  * measurement failures now report why (timeout / network / no index / decode
    / too few segments) instead of dumping an AbortError
  * drop the old onAudioError behaviour that jumped to list index 1
