i0/i1/i2.hdslb.com are replicas of the same object store (verified: the same
/bfs/archive/*.jpg returns byte-identical content from all three), yet a single
shard can be unreachable from a given network. The player then shows a missing
cover and the console fills up with ERR_CONNECTION_TIMED_OUT even though
playback is fine.

A capture-phase `error` listener swaps the hostname for another shard (max two
extra tries per <img>), which covers every cover in the app at once.
