From 3b3a89a05d1a716c5f1405541ecf0a56834dddad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: loudness-agent <agent@example.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:16:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] feat(failover): remember dead hosts, probe instead of
 waiting

The previous failover still felt broken on a network that cannot reach one
whole CDN bucket: every mirror lived on the same unreachable host, and each
retry waited for the media element's own ~30s connect timeout.

  * hosts that failed are remembered (timeout: 60s, hard connect failure: 10
    minutes) and forgotten again as soon as a probe succeeds, so a bad bucket
    is not waited on twice
  * probes are concurrent 2KB range requests with a 2.5s budget, so picking a
    live mirror takes ~3s instead of minutes
  * the stall watchdog drops from 20s to 8s and probes the current line first,
    so a merely slow host is not skipped by mistake
  * resolution already avoids known-bad hosts: swap to a live mirror up front,
    or fail fast (skip in ~1s) when the host cannot connect at all
