The player, B站's own loudness levelling and the Bilibili_LoudNorm userscript can
all end up fighting over the same volume. This adds a single switch that makes
sure only *this* player's loudness normalization may touch the audio:

  * new `loudnessExclusive` setting, default off, rendered as the first switch of
    the loudness block; a floating badge shows 🔒/🔊 state in the player
  * exclusive mode forces the sampled measurement (never the whole-file ffmpeg
    pass), ignores B站's own loudness metadata and skips the legacy `r128gain`
    path that writes `audio.volume`
  * with the main loudness switch off, exclusive mode touches nothing at all:
    no Web Audio takeover, no measuring — plain raw passthrough
  * the settings panel now lists the currently effective audio chain, and the
    `r128gain` checkbox is greyed out while exclusive mode is on
